# Regime-Aware Market Intelligence Agent

The architecture is FROZEN as v2.1 — see `docs/architecture-v2.1-frozen.md`. The implementation
contract is `docs/phase2_build_spec.md` and it is authoritative for schemas, function signatures,
and tests.

## HARD RULES

1. Never introduce anything on the kill list in architecture doc §17: no model router, model tiers,
   AI Gateway, Model D, LLM-generated forecasting features, Delta→Lakebase serving sync, multi-agent
   systems, custom MCP servers, streaming, Kubernetes, microservices. Do not suggest them.
2. Statistical constraints in architecture doc §5 are mandatory: statsmodels transition matrices are
   LEFT-stochastic (columns = previous state, columns sum to 1); `exog_tvtp` must use news shifted by
   one trading day with an explicit ones column; only `filtered_marginal_probabilities` may be used in
   `src/models/` — never smoothed; regimes re-sorted by fitted variance after every fit; fallback
   ladder C→B→A on fit failure.
3. Spark only in `src/ingestion/` and `src/pipelines/`. `src/models/` is pure pandas/numpy/statsmodels
   — never import pyspark there. Estimation uses percent log returns (×100), rescaled before simulation.
4. Every pipeline write is a MERGE on the declared keys (prices: `ticker` + `trade_date`; news:
   `article_id` + `ticker`). Never blind INSERT.
5. No secrets in code, ever. Keys come from `dbutils.secrets` or env vars.
6. Write the tests specified in the build spec IN THE SAME task as the code they test. Code without
   its tests is incomplete.
7. Follow the repo layout in build spec B0 exactly. Notebooks are thin wrappers; all logic lives in
   `src/`.
8. When the spec is silent, choose the simplest working option and leave a TODO comment. Ask before
   adding any dependency not in `requirements.txt`.
